  {
    "alert_id": "ALERT_IBUPROFEN_TDF_NEPHRO_002",
    "title": "Ibuprofen plus TDF and hypertension increases renal risk",
    "message": "Guidelines note TDF can cause renal failure and tubular wasting, and that intercurrent illness with dehydration may worsen renal function in TDF patients. Patient uses over-the-counter ibuprofen PRN for back pain while on TDF, with hypertension (BP 146/94), trace proteinuria, and low phosphate. NSAIDs reduce renal perfusion and can compound TDF-associated nephrotoxicity. The clinician's plan recommends continuing PRN ibuprofen without flagging this risk. No renal protective alternative for pain is addressed.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Advise limiting or avoiding ibuprofen. Consider paracetamol-based pain management. Monitor renal function and phosphate closely given concurrent TDF use.",
